From 84b3cf40fdf8c5469580e47a6c45dbfe3b7f63b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:11:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 98/99] Evidence counters: who writes what the RSX reads, who
 calls a range, a frame's commands

For the native renderer's boundary: which code, on which thread, produces the
commands, measured rather than read off the disassembly. Development only;
everything is off unless its switch is set.

- PS3_ATTRIB_ST=<lo>-<hi>[,...] (ppu_loader.cpp): guest stores into a range
  counted by writer and thread; PS3_ATTRIB_CALL=<lo>-<hi>[,...] indirect calls
  into a range counted by target, caller and thread. A window
  (PS3_ATTRIB_FROM/_SECS), then PS3_ATTRIB_OUT. Every store goes out of line
  and every indirect call the full way while armed: slow, not for timing.
- PS3_ATTRIB_SHADOW=1: the last writer (function, thread, lr) of every word
  of the first store range, for the frame trace.
- RSX_FRAME_TRACE=<s>:<frames>:<path> (cellGcmSys.c): every command header the
  drain reads in N frames with its data words, and with the shadow the guest
  function, thread and caller that stored it.
- GCM_SEMA_STATS=1: the drain's NV406E acquires by label offset, and how many
  found their value already there.

On 3D Dot Game Heroes (2026-11-04): every store into RSX-visible memory and
every indirect call into asp or PPFX was on the main thread; a frame's 42,000
command headers were 82% asp, 16% PPFX, 2% game code through libgcm; the one
acquire a frame (label 0x10, WaitFlip) was always already satisfied.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
